# Cloudflare Pages redirects — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# NOTE: apex/www/cross-domain canonicalization (getsetcraft.com apex and the
# getsetcraft.net pair -> the canonical host) is NOT done here. Pages _redirects
# only reliably matches on PATH, not hostname, so host rules placed here do not
# fire. Canonicalize those with a Cloudflare Redirect Rule at the zone level
# (dashboard > the zone > Rules > Redirect Rules). Path redirects below work.

# The app download. As of 1.5.0 there are TWO builds, Apple Silicon and Intel, so
# /download can no longer be a straight redirect to one file: it now serves the
# chooser page, which pre-selects the right one and explains how to check.
#
# The /latest/ paths below are stable. Ship a release with assets named
# Setcraft-AppleSilicon.dmg and Setcraft-Intel.dmg and these follow automatically,
# no edit here needed. (The version lives in the git tag, not the filename, which
# is what keeps that true.)
# NOTE: there is deliberately NO rule for /download itself. Cloudflare Pages
# already serves public/download.html at /download, and it canonicalizes the other
# way too: a request for /download.html gets a 308 to /download. So a
# "/download -> /download.html" rule is not just redundant, it is an infinite
# redirect loop (verified live on 2026-07-27, and it broke every download on the
# site until it was removed). Let Pages serve the page; only map things that are
# NOT files here.
/download/apple-silicon   https://github.com/brianhaggis/setcraft-website/releases/latest/download/Setcraft-AppleSilicon.dmg  302
/download/intel           https://github.com/brianhaggis/setcraft-website/releases/latest/download/Setcraft-Intel.dmg  302

# Pre-1.5.0 installs and any link in the wild that still expects one file. Send it
# to the chooser rather than 404ing or guessing an architecture wrong.
/download/Setcraft.dmg    /download  302
